WEBVTT

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:10.300
Kaito!

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:12.090
This is bad! Right now,
we gotta run for it!

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:14.090
Kaito, go!

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:21.220
This is...

00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:27.050
Kaito...

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:31.500
He was swallowed up by the
Double Ring and ran wild.

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:33.190
I have to go.

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:35.600
Mr. Freecell!

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:45.370
Kaito, I won't let you die,

00:00:46.330 --> 00:00:48.500
not until you fulfill your promise to me.

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:08.000
Lost

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.130
Tesaguri de sagashiteta
I've searched, groping

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:15.050
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
The answer to a future that's been closed off

00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:16.970
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
Is nowhere to be found

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:20.300
Hashiru shoudou, ima kaidoku funou
The impulse to run, it's impossible to decipher now

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:22.010
Found

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:26.270
Kudaketa hazu no unmei o
A fate that was supposedly smashed

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:30.730
Mijuku na yume no naka de kikoeta kitanda
I've come to hear it within that half-formed dream:

00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:33.570
Saigo made I'll be there for you
Until the end, I'll be there for you

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:36.650
Tachidomaranai, kono hari dake wa
It won't stop, not this needle

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:39.990
Boku no asu o kizamu oto o tsukisasu
It will pierce the sound that engraves my tomorrow

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:41.910
Shinjitsu kara nigetara ima
If I run from the truth, then now...

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:43.620
Genjitsu ni mo maketara ima
If I lose to reality, then now...

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:45.950
Nani ga nokoru no?
What will remain?

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:48.170
(Nokoru no?)
(Will remain?)

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:50.540
Kazoekirenai kono kizu dake ga
These countless wounds of mine

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:54.000
Boku no kinou o zanzou to shite kataru
They tell of my yesterday as an afterimage

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.710
Unmei ga hodoketemo ima
Even if fate were unraveled, now...

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:57.550
Sonzai o kowashitemo ima
Even if my existence were smashed, now...

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:00.430
Boku no michi o yuku yo
I will travel my path

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:02.550
It's now or never

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:03.640
That is what they say

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:05.720
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:09.400
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:10.560
That is what they say

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:12.730
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:16.240
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:17.440
That is what they say

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:19.860
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:26.000
The Awakening

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:34.320
Hyaaa!

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:36.970
Cube!

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.760
No..Nonoha...

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:41.440
You all right?

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:44.320
Somehow.

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:48.430
Th..That's...

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:03.870
There they are!

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:05.880
Gammon and Ana!

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:08.520
They're both all right,

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:12.900
but it looks like they're
blocked in and can't move.

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:14.360
And Kaito?

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.300
No sign of him.

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:22.320
Found him! It's Kaito!

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:24.410
Sure enough...

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:28.370
When that collapsed, he fell
down to the lowest level.

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:31.980
Is Kaito all right?

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:36.000
Judging by his brainwaves,
it looks like he's unconscious.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.800
We have to hurry and help him.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:38.480
Impossible!

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:42.990
The collapsed fragments have
piled up on top of him.

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:48.060
What's more, Yoshio couldn't
clear all that rubble.

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:49.310
Come on!

00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:52.310
Isn't there some way to reach Kaito?

00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:53.710
Hold on.

00:03:57.440 --> 00:03:58.440
This is...

00:03:58.440 --> 00:03:59.820
What is it?

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:01.110
I don't know,

00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:05.470
but it looks like this structure
leads down to Kaito's level.

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:09.840
If we follow it, we might
be able to reach him.

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:12.640
I have to go.

00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:15.850
I'm going to go help Kaito.

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:19.460
I can carry him and find
my way back here somehow.

00:04:19.460 --> 00:04:21.240
Wait, I'll go too!

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:24.740
Cube, you help Ana and Gammon.

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:28.500
They'll need Yoshio's strength
to rescue them, right?

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:30.630
But...

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:34.690
It's okay.

00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:38.710
I've already memorized
the map you plotted out.

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:41.800
Believe in my memory, and in my muscle.

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:44.680
All right.

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:47.450
Take care of Kaito.

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:48.430
You bet!

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:53.080
Be careful, Nonoha.

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:55.440
We'll help Gammon and Ana.

00:04:56.500 --> 00:04:58.500
Wait, don't tell me this...

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:03.510
It's a puzzle!

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:08.860
What do I do?

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:12.160
I have to go through this to go down?

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:19.820
Do your best, Nonoha Itou.

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:24.130
You're the only one who can help Kaito!

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:29.100
Ka..Kaito, here I come.

00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:31.550
That's impossible for you.

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:33.020
You!

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:39.230
Kaito's alive, isn't he?

00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:42.260
Just wait, Kaito.

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:44.440
I'm coming to save you.

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:47.770
Save Kaito?

00:05:48.050 --> 00:05:49.680
Don't make me laugh.

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:52.370
You're the one who put Kaito in danger!

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:03.420
The force of the cave-in
has made this whole area fragile.

00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:06.220
A giant wooden cross puzzle, eh?

00:06:06.650 --> 00:06:09.760
Herbert's creations are
always so wasteful.

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:13.970
Still, thanks to that, we
can reach Kaito's location.

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:17.000
We can't see the whole structure.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:18.800
That makes it difficult to solve.

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:21.520
I know the structure.

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:23.710
Cube mapped it out,

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:26.220
this puzzle and where Kaito is.

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:27.400
It's all in my head.

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:30.240
Huh?

00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:35.080
I can't trust you.

00:06:36.020 --> 00:06:40.580
But if you really will help Kaito...

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:52.980
It's a memento of my mama.

00:06:53.620 --> 00:06:57.930
To me, it's as important as
the promise made with Kaito.

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:00.790
Is this enough for you to trust me?

00:07:03.130 --> 00:07:04.160
All right.

00:07:08.140 --> 00:07:10.600
They're challenging that puzzle?

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:15.120
I look forward to obtaining
some splendid data.

00:07:16.810 --> 00:07:18.120
Shall we begin?

00:07:18.520 --> 00:07:21.150
The block that we're standing on now...

00:07:21.850 --> 00:07:24.150
Can you tell where it connects to?

00:07:24.150 --> 00:07:24.930
Huh?

00:07:26.900 --> 00:07:28.320
Uh...

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:30.380
Probably over there.

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:34.870
All right...

00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:46.420
In..Incredible!

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:51.820
And that?

00:07:52.180 --> 00:07:53.590
Eh?

00:07:54.760 --> 00:07:56.180
Um...

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:09.690
Incredible...

00:08:09.690 --> 00:08:11.310
He does it so easily.

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:14.220
Say...

00:08:14.780 --> 00:08:18.510
Are you really trying to help Kaito?

00:08:20.410 --> 00:08:21.870
Of course.

00:08:21.870 --> 00:08:23.870
I can't let Kaito die,

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:26.520
not until he fulfills his promise to me.

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:33.110
Pinochle said something.

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:36.850
He said he didn't know
how your mother's death

00:08:36.850 --> 00:08:42.120
and Kaito breaking his
promise were related.

00:08:43.390 --> 00:08:45.690
Kaito's wanted to know this whole time.

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:47.690
Just what did he do?

00:08:47.690 --> 00:08:51.370
Kaito came here because he wants
to remember more about you!

00:08:54.450 --> 00:08:57.140
Please, tell me the truth!

00:08:57.620 --> 00:08:58.830
Did Kaito...

00:08:58.830 --> 00:09:01.080
Was your mama really...

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:03.140
Don't go getting the wrong idea.

00:09:03.790 --> 00:09:08.040
You and I are cooperating
to save Kaito, that's all.

00:09:08.590 --> 00:09:10.380
You're not my friend,

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:12.260
and this is nothing to discuss with you.

00:09:13.170 --> 00:09:16.030
I know that, but...

00:09:16.930 --> 00:09:18.000
Well, fine.

00:09:19.010 --> 00:09:23.060
Kaito has trampled on
the memories of my mama,

00:09:23.060 --> 00:09:26.000
and on his promise to me.

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:38.360
I was always so enthralled with Kaito.

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:43.330
He would approach any
puzzle without hesitation,

00:09:43.330 --> 00:09:44.390
and solve it.

00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:57.780
H..He got them all right.

00:10:00.050 --> 00:10:03.290
That spark, that strength,
that nobility...

00:10:03.890 --> 00:10:05.540
They were all so bright.

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:08.170
If I could be friends with Kaito,

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:10.200
then maybe I would change.

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:15.400
He might set me free.

00:10:15.990 --> 00:10:17.420
That's what I thought.

00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:32.670
Set free?

00:10:33.300 --> 00:10:34.070
From what?

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:39.910
Well, no matter.

00:10:44.390 --> 00:10:46.140
That's why I was happy,

00:10:46.890 --> 00:10:49.420
when we made that promise
to solve a puzzle together.

00:10:49.940 --> 00:10:52.310
Huh? A puzzle, together?

00:10:53.270 --> 00:10:57.050
Sure! Okay, see you Sunday.

00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:08.710
Mama!

00:11:08.710 --> 00:11:11.560
Kaito said he'd do a puzzle with me!

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:14.320
We made a promise!

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:17.320
But...

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:24.720
Kaito never came.

00:11:26.760 --> 00:11:30.140
He broke his promise to me.

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:34.590
And that same day,

00:11:35.280 --> 00:11:37.280
my beloved mama died.

00:11:52.400 --> 00:11:54.940
While I was waiting for Kaito,

00:11:54.940 --> 00:11:57.280
Mama's condition suddenly worsened,

00:11:58.060 --> 00:12:00.450
and then she breathed her last breath.

00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:07.100
How cruel, to abandon
my sick mama to go play.

00:12:07.100 --> 00:12:08.810
I was an ungrateful child.

00:12:08.810 --> 00:12:10.080
That's what they said.

00:12:52.390 --> 00:12:53.580
What is it?

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:56.970
My mama's death...

00:12:58.610 --> 00:12:59.960
It wasn't Kaito's fault.

00:13:03.520 --> 00:13:06.530
I let my mama die.

00:13:21.580 --> 00:13:23.820
H..Hold on!

00:13:25.030 --> 00:13:28.590
I could never make very good puzzles.

00:13:29.180 --> 00:13:31.490
I wasn't the best student,
and Mama hated me.

00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:33.790
And I...

00:13:36.270 --> 00:13:39.500
I despised my mama.

00:13:48.130 --> 00:13:51.100
This memory is a lie.

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:55.180
This memory...

00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:57.020
is the real one.

00:13:59.360 --> 00:14:00.800
I've remembered.

00:14:01.550 --> 00:14:02.900
All of it.

00:14:04.010 --> 00:14:05.150
What are you talking about?

00:14:05.550 --> 00:14:07.530
You're saying this is the truth?

00:14:10.220 --> 00:14:12.560
What is this?

00:14:12.560 --> 00:14:14.200
I don't get it!

00:14:14.770 --> 00:14:17.420
So, everything you've
told Kaito up till now

00:14:17.420 --> 00:14:19.560
has been a lie?!

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:22.640
That's just ridiculous!

00:14:25.350 --> 00:14:26.590
"Ridiculous"?

00:14:27.330 --> 00:14:28.520
Could be.

00:14:30.840 --> 00:14:34.080
But I didn't think so,

00:14:34.080 --> 00:14:35.750
not till just now.

00:14:35.750 --> 00:14:37.620
But they're your memories!

00:14:37.620 --> 00:14:38.580
What are you...

00:14:40.290 --> 00:14:43.600
The Ring can distort thoughts,
overwriting memory.

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:46.720
He hated his "beloved" mama.

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:48.970
It wasn't Kaito who killed her.

00:14:48.970 --> 00:14:51.860
Yet he made everything Kaito's fault.

00:14:53.060 --> 00:14:55.160
What does that mean?

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:59.840
What have you said that's
true, and what is a lie?

00:15:00.450 --> 00:15:04.590
Could it be, even this "promise"
with Kaito is made up?

00:15:04.590 --> 00:15:06.090
The promise is...

00:15:06.660 --> 00:15:07.770
True.

00:15:09.130 --> 00:15:12.910
That promise alone is all
that's been keeping me alive.

00:15:13.790 --> 00:15:16.660
A promise that, for me, was sacred.

00:15:16.660 --> 00:15:19.080
It was everything to me!

00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:22.660
If you would defile that promise...

00:15:23.340 --> 00:15:25.020
you'll be given no mercy.

00:15:29.720 --> 00:15:32.090
Self-repair of altered memories...

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:35.450
Control of the emotional
areas of the brain...

00:15:36.390 --> 00:15:41.520
It seems this upgrade has
increased the Ring's stability.

00:15:42.700 --> 00:15:45.340
Oh, my, you're still here, Whi?

00:15:49.280 --> 00:15:51.150
Miss Melancholy...

00:15:51.150 --> 00:15:53.330
That's an unusual combination.

00:15:54.280 --> 00:15:56.580
They're being friendly, solving a puzzle?

00:15:56.580 --> 00:15:57.100
Yes.

00:15:57.850 --> 00:16:00.070
We've been receiving
some splendid numbers.

00:16:00.780 --> 00:16:05.490
Sure enough, the forced activation rate
of Mr. Freecell's brain

00:16:05.490 --> 00:16:08.610
increases dramatically only
when Kaito Daimon is involved.

00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:13.980
Having you scout Mr. Freecell
was indeed the right choice.

00:16:18.710 --> 00:16:20.330
Huh? Transfer?

00:16:20.980 --> 00:16:22.270
You didn't know?

00:16:22.270 --> 00:16:23.940
He went back to Japan.

00:16:23.940 --> 00:16:27.180
They say he'll be goin'
to Root Gakuen now.

00:16:31.580 --> 00:16:32.990
That's right...

00:16:42.590 --> 00:16:44.120
He's gone...

00:16:44.980 --> 00:16:46.190
Kaito...

00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:51.300
In the end, I couldn't talk to him
even once after that day.

00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:54.940
Cruel, isn't he? Kaito Daimon?

00:16:56.510 --> 00:17:00.540
Running off without keeping
his promise to you.

00:17:02.560 --> 00:17:05.710
U..Um, who are you people?

00:17:06.980 --> 00:17:10.210
The Orpheus Order.

00:17:14.450 --> 00:17:16.970
Scouting Freecell was the right choice?

00:17:17.700 --> 00:17:20.020
I hope that's really the case.

00:17:26.620 --> 00:17:27.980
Wh..What's that?

00:17:28.380 --> 00:17:30.050
It's starting to collapse.

00:17:30.050 --> 00:17:30.860
Hurry!

00:17:31.380 --> 00:17:34.150
Which block does this one connect to?

00:17:34.420 --> 00:17:35.280
Um...

00:17:35.720 --> 00:17:36.600
Too slow!

00:17:38.350 --> 00:17:39.120
I see it.

00:17:46.480 --> 00:17:47.370
I have to go,

00:17:48.190 --> 00:17:49.210
to where Kaito is.

00:17:49.650 --> 00:17:51.280
W..Wait!

00:17:54.570 --> 00:17:55.920
Th..This is...

00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:03.520
H..Hold on!

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:04.620
What's going on?

00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:08.440
I haven't been telling you
anything about the puzzle.

00:18:18.040 --> 00:18:19.490
This means he's already learned

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:21.570
everything about the puzzle, huh?

00:18:21.570 --> 00:18:22.870
Impossible!

00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:25.500
You're saying his brain's forced
activation rate can't be measured?!

00:18:25.900 --> 00:18:28.250
These readings, they look like...

00:18:29.400 --> 00:18:30.180
What?!

00:18:32.190 --> 00:18:33.170
What is it?

00:18:33.560 --> 00:18:36.130
Data transfer from the Ring has ceased.

00:18:37.490 --> 00:18:39.840
Why can't I assume control of it?!

00:18:40.910 --> 00:18:41.820
Ah...

00:18:42.950 --> 00:18:44.220
This is...

00:19:01.100 --> 00:19:04.160
Kaito, I've finally realized.

00:19:04.880 --> 00:19:07.660
We didn't need fake reasons,

00:19:08.050 --> 00:19:10.400
or the past, or my mama,

00:19:10.400 --> 00:19:12.400
any of it.

00:19:13.110 --> 00:19:14.010
I can see it.

00:19:14.610 --> 00:19:15.480
I can see it!

00:19:27.500 --> 00:19:28.510
Our...

00:19:34.090 --> 00:19:34.990
future.

00:19:53.690 --> 00:19:55.460
Gammon! Ana!

00:19:55.980 --> 00:19:57.400
You okay?

00:19:57.400 --> 00:20:00.530
Yeah, somehow, Q-taro.

00:20:00.530 --> 00:20:02.720
Thanks for the help, Shio-Shio!

00:20:03.380 --> 00:20:05.160
What about Kaito and Nonoha?

00:20:05.160 --> 00:20:06.540
I'll explain later.

00:20:06.540 --> 00:20:07.600
This way!

00:20:21.010 --> 00:20:22.040
This is it.

00:20:38.230 --> 00:20:39.250
Kaito!

00:20:39.820 --> 00:20:42.520
Freecell, what're you
doin' here, dammit?!

00:20:43.040 --> 00:20:46.010
He... Freecell saved him.

00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:48.010
Saved Kaito.

00:20:49.180 --> 00:20:53.270
Thank you for trusting me, Nonoha Itou.

00:20:55.580 --> 00:20:56.520
Um...

00:20:57.410 --> 00:20:58.150
Here.

00:20:59.590 --> 00:21:01.030
I don't need it,

00:21:01.720 --> 00:21:02.520
not anymore.

00:21:03.800 --> 00:21:05.510
For me...

00:21:05.510 --> 00:21:08.140
The promise, my mama,

00:21:08.140 --> 00:21:09.660
none of it means anything.

00:21:10.420 --> 00:21:11.410
After all...

00:21:13.520 --> 00:21:17.420
I know now, many different things.

00:21:18.230 --> 00:21:20.920
You're watching, aren't you, Whist?

00:21:21.940 --> 00:21:24.150
This poor excuse of a fake....

00:21:25.140 --> 00:21:27.050
I've made it into the real thing!

00:21:27.820 --> 00:21:31.560
Sorry for ruining your little plan, huh?

00:21:32.080 --> 00:21:35.080
That Ring is real?

00:21:35.870 --> 00:21:37.710
What does that mean?

00:21:38.380 --> 00:21:39.320
Kaito!

00:21:41.420 --> 00:21:42.380
Are you all right?

00:21:42.800 --> 00:21:43.570
Kaito!

00:21:45.270 --> 00:21:48.430
Kaito, you want to save me, don't you?

00:21:48.900 --> 00:21:53.080
If you win a game against
me, this Ring can come off.

00:21:53.610 --> 00:21:57.810
But you can't beat me as you are now.

00:21:57.810 --> 00:21:59.590
After all, I'm...

00:22:05.360 --> 00:22:09.160
Become much, much stronger, Kaito!

00:22:09.160 --> 00:22:12.220
Once you do, it can begin...

00:22:12.220 --> 00:22:13.390
Our puzzle time!

00:22:15.160 --> 00:22:17.310
Freecell...

00:22:18.210 --> 00:22:18.980
Kaito!

00:22:19.290 --> 00:22:21.000
Hey, hang in there!

00:22:21.000 --> 00:22:21.880
Kaito!

00:22:21.880 --> 00:22:22.710
Kaito!
Kaito!

00:22:23.380 --> 00:22:25.230
Hold on, Kaito!

00:22:25.720 --> 00:22:27.550
Kaito!

00:22:38.710 --> 00:22:40.050
Eiyuukidori
Playing the hero

00:22:40.050 --> 00:22:44.940
Itsudatte shinjita muteki no kankaku
A sense of invincibility you always believed in

00:22:45.550 --> 00:22:51.370
Tatakatte iru no wa chikyuu no tame nanka ja nai
You're not fighting for the sake of the world or anything

00:22:51.370 --> 00:22:54.160
Motto maipeesu de
It's for a more leisurely

00:22:54.160 --> 00:22:59.230
Sou, motto shoujiki na onegai no tame
Yeah, more straightforward request

00:22:59.600 --> 00:23:07.670
Nandotonaku kizutsuitemo tachiagare, hero
Even if you're wounded over and over, rise up, hero

00:23:07.670 --> 00:23:13.220
Kitto daijoubu, kimi o mamorunda
It's sure to be all right, I'll protect you

00:23:13.610 --> 00:23:17.040
Machigai da to shitemo tomarenai
Even if it's wrong, it can't be stopped

00:23:17.040 --> 00:23:20.650
Seikai ka nante wakaranai
I don't know if it's the right answer

00:23:21.550 --> 00:23:24.660
Donna toki demo original ni
No matter the situation

00:23:24.660 --> 00:23:27.400
Step o fumidashiteku
I'll take those first steps, originally

00:23:27.400 --> 00:23:30.770
Dramatic ni, mawaru sekai de
On this spinning world, I'm searching, dramatically

00:23:30.770 --> 00:23:34.430
Kiwameita wonder sagashiteru
For wonders that sparkle

00:23:35.190 --> 00:23:38.430
Boku, shijou saikou no tabi o tsuzukeyou
Me, I'll keep going on the greatest journey in history

00:23:38.430 --> 00:23:42.740
Image shite shiawase na mirai e
To the happy future I imagined

00:23:44.430 --> 00:23:46.060
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:47.920 --> 00:23:51.380
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:51.380 --> 00:23:52.800
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:54.710 --> 00:23:56.260
(Mirai e)
(To the future)

00:24:02.250 --> 00:24:06.360
Master Rook, it seems Kaito Daimon
has asked for puzzle training.

00:24:06.360 --> 00:24:10.110
Yes, I've prepared something for Kaito.

00:24:10.110 --> 00:24:11.740
A very dangerous puzzle.

00:24:11.740 --> 00:24:13.990
What sort of puzzle is it?

00:24:13.990 --> 00:24:15.780
It's incredibly shocking.

00:24:15.780 --> 00:24:17.830
Yes, one that could crush him.

00:24:17.830 --> 00:24:20.500
Next time, "The Puzzle
